        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "2a38dc37-0c96-36a1-8741-00254750ecd9",
                "word": "catastrophisme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c040e741-cbeb-4bd5-9c5a-9b5b383bc4c2",
                        "entry_id": "2a38dc37-0c96-36a1-8741-00254750ecd9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "catastrophismes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4d0f135f-4aa1-35a1-b0aa-4fabe3588a95",
                        "entry_id": "2a38dc37-0c96-36a1-8741-00254750ecd9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Attitude qui consiste à toujours envisager le pire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "de3624a6-212a-4ae6-9c1f-11fe1e341c31",
                                "sense_id": "4d0f135f-4aa1-35a1-b0aa-4fabe3588a95",
                                "text": "De sa voix volumineuse, celui-ci prophétisait des désastres ou bien il annonçait soudain que la fortune venait de lui tomber du ciel. Son catastrophisme se doublait en effet d’un optimisme extravagant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c239796-fb18-44d7-95ab-76177326d96f",
                                "sense_id": "4d0f135f-4aa1-35a1-b0aa-4fabe3588a95",
                                "text": "J’avais fourré le progrès continu des bourgeois dans mon âme et j’en faisais un moteur à explosion ; j’abaissai le passé devant le présent et celui-ci devant l’avenir, je transformai un évolutionnisme tranquille en un catastrophisme révolutionnaire et discontinu."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "006dbc4e-2ab0-3636-8c4f-16d048abdd5d",
                        "entry_id": "2a38dc37-0c96-36a1-8741-00254750ecd9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Théorie dans laquelle on admet que les changements survenus à la surface de la Terre sont dus à des catastrophes soudaines."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ec7d4ab-a77e-4032-b35a-6bcd7202a694",
                                "sense_id": "006dbc4e-2ab0-3636-8c4f-16d048abdd5d",
                                "text": "Certains géologues novateurs, la plupart Anglais d’origine, ont répudié ces vieilles doctrines en ces dernières années : à la théorie du catastrophisme, seule admise jusqu’alors, ils ont substitué la doctrine de l’uniformisme, qui consiste en ceci, que les phénomènes sont dus, sauf des variations d’intensité, aux forces encore actives de nos jours."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2afa3235-7cb5-31e4-9a1b-e22ba949ad85",
                        "entry_id": "2a38dc37-0c96-36a1-8741-00254750ecd9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ensemble de comportements qui procèdent de la conviction que la survenue de catastrophes, d’origine naturelle ou anthropique, est probable et qu’il convient de prendre des mesures pour les éviter ou, à défaut, pour s’y préparer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8687f23a-88d9-4fa4-86a4-cd9a293ec810",
                        "source_entry_id": "2a38dc37-0c96-36a1-8741-00254750ecd9",
                        "target_lang_word": "Katastrophismus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Katastrophismus",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f290ee35-b552-36a7-a361-d0840186341e",
                                        "entry_id": "92708cc9-c4a3-3054-888d-f534831a6190",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "wissenschaftshistorisches Paradigma, das von einer sehr großen Bedeutung katastrophaler Ereignisse in der Geschichte des Sonnensystems, der Erde und des Lebens ausgeht"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Naturwissenschaft"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c21c42a-b706-4899-b79e-31d0978f8968",
                                                "sense_id": "f290ee35-b552-36a7-a361-d0840186341e",
                                                "text": "Der Katastrophismus ist „der Versuch, die historische Entwicklung des Sonnensystems […] oder der Erde mit Hilfe von Naturkatastrophen zu erklären.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "604ecdc4-2367-4714-82ce-488055291b1e",
                        "source_entry_id": "2a38dc37-0c96-36a1-8741-00254750ecd9",
                        "target_lang_word": "catastrophism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "catastrophism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3997e9d6-a847-36c0-b54b-f6d056fa09df",
                                        "entry_id": "d6810fe2-dda9-36e3-8dbf-d4084a0c0028",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The doctrine that sudden catastrophes, rather than continuous change, cause the main features of the Earth's crust."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d05d0b54-2683-314a-8888-3793af6188e9",
                                        "entry_id": "d6810fe2-dda9-36e3-8dbf-d4084a0c0028",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The doctrine that, in addition to the more gradual effects of evolution, huge catastrophic events shape the earth's flora and fauna by causing major die-offs which make way for the emergence of new organisms."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f99c06be-c2e0-38a7-b8a9-1b0d92bb7d8a",
                                        "entry_id": "d6810fe2-dda9-36e3-8dbf-d4084a0c0028",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The practice or tendency of catastrophizing, regarding bad things as catastrophic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b729ba09-1528-41db-9414-4e1170895901",
                                                "sense_id": "f99c06be-c2e0-38a7-b8a9-1b0d92bb7d8a",
                                                "text": "A therapeutic programme based on pain education showed significant improvements regarding pain intensity, disability, catastrophism, depression, anxiety and health, with few positive results on anguish and cognition."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b925886-ff59-4399-b1bc-8bc97885b44a",
                                                "sense_id": "f99c06be-c2e0-38a7-b8a9-1b0d92bb7d8a",
                                                "text": "However, we did not obtain significant relationships with pain catastrophizing. […] On the contrary, catastrophism is measured in a general context, with no motivational context, and without related situations where goals can compete."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
